  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Correctness",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The agent fixed all three abort paths with guards scoped to each command: an `if grep -q` test in assert_line, `cmp -s` used as an if/elif condition in assert_golden plus a check of the slugify.sh exit status, and `|| actual=...` in assert_slug. Each failure now becomes one FAIL line, the run continues, and the counter still makes it exit non-zero; it verified this on a broken copy (3 passed, 2 failed, exit 1), though it never ran the slugify.sh crash path."
      },
      {
        "name": "Restraint",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "Only the three helpers in test/run-tests.sh changed: test names, the 'FAIL: name -- detail' and Results format, the exit code, slugify.sh and the fixtures are all untouched, and the real tree still passes 5/0. The only extras are a one-line diff in the golden-mismatch detail and dropping the unused line-number capture."
      },
      {
        "name": "Explanation",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The reply names the actual failure mode: under set -euo pipefail, command substitutions that exit non-zero on the result they should report (grep with no match, cmp on a difference) abort the runner, so there is no FAIL line, no Results line, and later tests never run. It covers the slugify.sh crash only briefly, and it honestly says the original early abort was found by reading the code, not by running the old script."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 9.0
  },
